[38;2;124;124;124mBetween two matched pairs $\{u, v\}$ and $\{x, y\}$: we can have edges $u$-$x$, [0m[38;2;124;124;124m$u$-$y$, $v$-$x$, $v$-$y$, but with the constraint that $u$ and $v$ share no [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mcommon neighbor. So if $x$ is adjacent to $u$, then $x$ cannot be adjacent to [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$v$. Similarly for $y$. And if $u$ is adjacent to $x$, then $u$ cannot be [0m
[38;2;124;124;124madjacent to... wait, the constraint is per-pair.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFor pair $\{u, v\}$: every vertex outside $\{u, v\}$ is adjacent to at most one [0m[38;2;124;124;124mof $u, v$.[0m

